{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_c001dfc6-7212-4726-9589-a18061bcfeed","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nDeliverable written and validated at 573s of the 600s budget (`specialist_done.json` + `.partial.json`, both identical payloads).\n\n## What the recon found\n\n**Process finding first:** the live tree is **not** the one in my hint list. `/usr/local/bin/vllm-wu1w` launches `/opt/envs/wu1w/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm`, which is a *differently-patched* copy of `/opt/envs/vllm/...`. Recon against the hinted root would have wrongly concluded AITER INT8 is dead here.\n\n**The central un-bridged switch.** `is_aiter_found_and_supported()` returns `get_cdna_version() > 2`, and gfx90a returns exactly `2` → `False`. That feeds the `@if_aiter_supported` decorator, which on `False` returns **`None`** (falsy, silently — not an error) for **22 predicates** including `is_mha_enabled`, `are_gdn_triton_kernels_available`, `is_triton_unified_attn_enabled`, `is_tgemm_enabled`. Only **two** got the gfx90a carve-out (`is_aiter_attention_supported()` → `on_gfx9()`, itself a gfx90a-inclusive helper that already exists in the tree): `is_linear_enabled()` and `register_ops_once()`. The class docstring even claims the decorator checks `is_on_gfx9()` — the code does not.\n\n**Highest-value candidate (proposal 1, marked `atomic`):** the AITER fused GDN decode path is blocked *twice* — once by that umbrella (so `GDN_AITER_TRITON_AVAILABLE=False`, and the aiter kernels are in fact installed in amd_aiter-0.1.19), and again by `gqa_interleaved_layout` hardcoded `False` at `qwen3_5.py:148`. 48 of 64 layers are GDN and the workload is decode-dominated, so this is the biggest ceiling on the box.\n\n**Deduplicated two near-misses** into one patch rather than proposing both: the CDNA3 umbrella is fixed once in `_aiter_ops.py`, and the Qwen3.5 layout remap is a second, separately-sufficient change.\n\n**Negative result worth recording:** the fused CUDA/hip GDN decode is *genuinely absent*, not gated — the tree already ships a `fused_gdn_hip` bridge, but the module/symbol doesn't exist (0 hits in `_C.abi3.so`). I flagged explicitly that **`VLLM_GDN_DECODE_KERNEL=cuda` must not be benched as a variant**: the guard hard-`ValueError`s when the env var is set explicitly instead of falling back, so it would fail the launch rather than measure anything.\n\n**Zero-patch probes (proposals 2–3):** `--attention-backend TRITON_ATTN` to A/B against the cPA-rejection fallback (head_size=256 is the *sole* failing conjunct — gqa_ratio 6 is in range; the log warning omits the reason, which is why it reads as a hardware limit), and `VLLM_ENABLE_FLA_PACKED_RECURRENT_DECODE=0` to de-risk the GDN direction by testing whether kernel choice matters at all here.\n\n**Scoped out by evidence:** the baseline log shows `AiterInt8ScaledMMLinearKernel` *is* selected and `rms_norm=['aiter','native']` is set, so the INT8 GEMM dispatch is already on its fast path — any further GEMM-backend proposal would have been redundant padding. Likewise I kept `ROCM_AITER_FA` off the list since head_dim=256 puts it outside the ASM FA coverage (consistent with platform law 11), and noted that a *blanket* change to `is_aiter_found_and_supported()` would be unsafe because it would also flip on AITER fused-MoE, which is documented-dead on gfx90a.\n\nI stayed read-only throughout: no patches, no benchmarks, no server launches. Two subagent fan-out attempts failed with API errors, so all source work was done inline."}],"model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0ba73e-8519-4c21-9b94-7ecf84646800","uuid":"ffb907ae-9e53-4a92-9d08-9f39ac7c0c26"}
